ConvertMe — third-party notices
================================

ConvertMe itself is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later (see `LICENSE`). It drives the following components. None of them is a
dependency of the Rust crates at build time; they are separate programs, bundled
with the installer or detected on the host at runtime.

Bundled programs
----------------

FFmpeg (`ffmpeg`, `ffprobe`)
    GPL v2 or later, built with libx264, libx265, libvpx, libaom, libopus,
    libvorbis, lame and libwebp.
    Source for the exact build shipped with each release is published at
    https://convertme.app/ffmpeg-source, and a written offer to supply the
    corresponding source on physical media is included in every installer.
    FFmpeg is invoked as a separate process; ConvertMe links no FFmpeg code.

ImageMagick (`magick`)
    ImageMagick licence (Apache-2.0 compatible).
    https://imagemagick.org/script/license.php

Ghostscript (`gs`)
    AGPL v3. Invoked as a separate process over its command line, which the
    AGPL permits; the corresponding source is available at
    https://convertme.app/ghostscript-source and from Artifex.

qpdf (`qpdf`)
    Apache-2.0. https://qpdf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/license.html

Poppler (`pdftoppm`, `pdftotext`)
    GPL v2 or later. https://poppler.freedesktop.org

Pandoc (`pandoc`)
    GPL v2 or later. https://pandoc.org

7-Zip (`7zz`)
    GNU LGPL v2.1, with the unRAR restriction: the unRAR code is used only to
    decode RAR archives, never to create them.

Tesseract (`tesseract`) and the `eng` traineddata
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract

The PDF sidecar (`convertme-pdf`)
    Python program bundled as a single executable. It uses:
      * PyMuPDF — AGPL v3, https://github.com/pymupdf/PyMuPDF
      * python-pptx — MIT
      * python-docx — MIT
      * openpyxl — MIT
    The sidecar runs as a separate process; its source is in `sidecars/pdf/` and
    is published at https://convertme.app/sidecar-source, satisfying the AGPL.

Detected, not bundled
---------------------

LibreOffice (`soffice`)
    MPL-2.0. Used for Office → PDF and ODT conversions when the user has it
    installed. ConvertMe never ships it; the affected wheel segments are hidden
    when it is absent and Settings names the gap.

Optional model download
-----------------------

Face detection for redaction uses YuNet (`face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx`),
Apache-2.0, from the OpenCV model zoo. It is not shipped with the installer; the
user downloads it into the app data directory, and every redaction path works
without it (text detection uses Tesseract).

Note on the original sketch: the SCRFD-500M weights named there come from the
InsightFace model zoo, which is licensed for non-commercial research only. A
GPL binary cannot redistribute them, so a permissively licensed detector is used
instead.

